{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/256488-new-transmutations","id":256488,"title":"New Transmutations!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-13T21:57:23-07:00","id":256488,"title":"New Transmutations!","content":"I thought some new Transmutations might be in order to help make a Promethean's Pilgrimage a little bit more bearable. Let me know what you think. <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> IMMUNIZE: 00000</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A Promethean\u2019s s world is full of impossible things; mad occultists, monsters born from body parts, spirits for the other side of reality, Angles made from fire and glass. Even more so then the supernatural are those blessedly few mortals that have a strong enough will to interact with the Created and not grow to despise then. More importantly, sometimes one of the Created is forced to work or be within proximity to a mortal (especially if this is part of a Milestone). Whispered among the created is a powerful Transmutation that essentially blocks Disquiet to one or two people. Thus allowing the Created to finally create a connection with a human they so desperately wish to have.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> Prerequisite: Sooth Disquiet, Scapegoat</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cost: 3 Pyros and 1 willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Action: Extended</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dice Pool: Azoth + Disquietism + occult vs Resolve </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Effect:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The number of individuals a Created can Immunize is equal to his stamina. If another mortal is given this power, not only does it fail but anyone else the Created has successfully immunized will also loose their protection. The protection also ends if the mortal ever sees the Created\u2019s disfigurements.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The person this power is being used upon must not already be suffering from Disquiet for it to work. If someone is already under Disquiet, this ability halts its progression. The power requires the Created to touch their target. Once successful, the mortal will be able to interact with the Created, even leave and comeback, for a 12 hour period. The Created can prolong the immunity for another 12 hours by spending a point of Pyros and willpower. Nobody said making friends, especially if you're made up of dead human parts, was easy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Role Results:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dramatic Failure: The effect fails and the human suffers Disquiet two levels higher.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failure: nothing happens and the Pyros is wasted. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Success: The human is free to interact with the Promethean for the next 12 hours. During this time however, the human HERSELF gives off a low level Disquiet aura. Those around her react as if she were a Promethean. Use the Promethean\u2019s Azoth to determine Disquiet roles for the human. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Exceptional Success: The immunization last for 24 hours</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><br /> SENSE DISQUIET: 000</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Everybody succumbs to Disquiet, yes some are more resilient than others, but humans can only hold out for so long before a Created\u2019s unnatural aura drives those around him mad. This Transmutation allows the Created to detect who is suffering from Disquiet and how far along they are into the spiral of insanity. At the very least, this allows the Promethean enough warning time to leave an area before a mob forms.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cost: 1 Pyros</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Action: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dice Pool: Intelligence + Occult</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Role Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dramatic Failure: the Promethean gets the wrong impression about a target. Someone he sees as being free from Disquiet might be suffering from a Stage 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Failure: The Promethean detects noting.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Success: The Promethean can tell who is suffering from Disquiet and who is not. This comes across and a black haze over individuals, as if they are caught in a light smog.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Exceptional success: The Promethean can gain greater detail regarding the severity of Disquiet. Those caught in the later stages ave a thicker and more pronounced haze then those in a lesser stage</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T00:35:40-07:00","id":256556,"title":"","content":"Immunize seems needless in light of the existence of Quell Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T22:15:41-07:00","id":257000,"title":"","content":"Quell Disquiet only works in an enclosed area. And then if more than the allotted persons enters the area, the effect fails","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T23:27:12-07:00","id":257010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingme1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/256488-new-transmutations?p=257000#post257000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quell Disquiet only works in an enclosed area.</div> </div> </div> </div>It works on a limited number of <i>people</i>, which nevertheless is of greater utility than a power that only works on one person and fails outright if you spend Pyros at all in their presence. Personal visits can generally be relied upon not to have more than one or two extra people show up out of the blue.<br /> <br /> 1e Transmutations have a number of problems as written, but a five-dot power with two prerequisites, a nonsensical dicepool, and an incessant Willpower drain is not what I would call a marked improvement over a similar power that's called out as one of the capstones of its discipline of Transmutation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T00:31:26-07:00","id":257022,"title":"","content":"Would Quell Disquiet work on, let's say, 3 individuals in a crowded area? What I would like to see is for some ability for a Promethean to have a human connection without such constraints. Even Frankenstine befriended a blind old man (yes he was blind, but there was still a connection) and a little girl (who he did kill, but didn't get the connection between throwing a girl into the water and a flower)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}